      ":question/problem": "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\int_{1}^{2}\\sech 4x\\tanh 4x\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=4x$. Then $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. When $x=1$, $u=4$; when $x=2$, $u=8$.\n\nUsing $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\sech u=-\\sech u\\tanh u$,\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_1^2\\sech(4x)\\tanh(4x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=\\frac{1}{4}\\int_{4}^{8}\\sech u\\tanh u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{4}[-\\sech u]_{4}^{8} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{4}(\\sech 4-\\sech 8).\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe integrand is continuous on $[1,2]$, and the result is positive because $\\sech u$ decreases for $u>0$.",
